Note: `householdId` is not mapped here via an expression; it is set on the `Owner` transient field in the controller (`OwnerRestControllerV1.getOwner` line 98 and `addOwner` line 126) before mapping, and carried through by MapStruct's name-matched mapping.

### Schema — `OwnerDto` field definitions
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`, the Owner schema (composed with OwnerFields). Relevant identity fields with line numbers:
- `memberId` (2157-2162): "'<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>' … CHK a single Luhn check digit over the digits of '<REGION><FY><HASH8>'." example `NSW26ABCD12345`
- `fiscalYear` (2163-2168): "'FY<YY>'", example `FY26`
- `householdId` (2169-2176): "Stable identifier shared by owners … same last name and address."
- `membershipPoints` (2188-2198), `membershipLevel` (2199-2208)
- `locality` (2209-2217): city-to-region table, example `NSW`
- `ownerSegment` (2218-2227): "'<TIER>_<AREA>' … PREMIUM when membershipLevel is 3 or more … METRO when locality is NSW/VIC/QLD", example `STANDARD_METRO`
- `timezone` (2228-2236): region-to-timezone table, example `Australia/Sydney`
- `contactPreference` (2262-2268), `telephoneDisplay` (2269-2276)
- `identityKey` (2277-2286): documented as `'normalizedTelephone|email|householdId'`, example `'+61412345678||'` (does not match the hashing implementation, see note above).

The owner segment builder itself is `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Segments.java`:
```java
